{"n": 254, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "254.webp", "text": "Correcting:\n\nA new adjustment will be necessary, if the\ntest value* can no longer be reached.\n\nTo loosen the injection pump, remove the\ndial gage and holder.\n\nUnscrew bolts (3 ... 5)\n\nLoosen nuts (1 and 2) only one half turn to\navoid tension from the toothed belt,\n\nApply dial gage with holder.\n\nMove injection pump to correct position\nSwinging the injection pump toward the\nengine = earlier ignition timing point\n\nTighten bolts in order of 1 through 5 after\nfinishing adjustments\nRecheck adjustment\n\n* See Specifications\n\n— Full throttle volume correction —\n\nwith full throttle smoke above 2500 rpm\n\n— Check compression — see 11 00 039.\n\n— Adjust valve clearance ~ see 11 34 004\n\n= Check static adjustment of injectron pump,\nUnscrew lock nut (1) and turn back up to\nlockplate (2).\n\nLockplate (2) limits the adjustment in direction\nof “‘more volume”.\n\nThe factory adjustment is marked with a notch\nand serves as an initial basis — remark the\ninitial position if necessary.\n\nAdjusting screw (3) must be “tightened” 3 and\n1/2 wrns with Special Tool 13 5 100.\nReference Values:\n\nScrew tightened = “less volume”\n\nScrew loosened = “more volume”\n\n3 and 1/2 turns of the adjusting screw will\nchange the volume by approx. 1.0 mm3.\n\nTighten lock nut (1),\n\nCaution!\n\nDanger of breaking the plastic housing —\ncounterhold on volume screw (4) if necessary!\nMake visual inspection after test drive — take\nback full throttle volume by another 1 mm3 if\nnecessary\n\nLock nut (1) with identification paint* *.\n\n** Source: HWB, No. 8122 9 407 404", "words": [["Correcting:", 0.2604, 0.0637, 0.3136, 0.0776], ["A", 0.2604, 0.0809, 0.2675, 0.0908], ["new", 0.2715, 0.0836, 0.2908, 0.0908], ["adjustment", 0.2943, 0.0809, 0.347, 0.0935], ["will", 0.3506, 0.0816, 0.3678, 0.0915], ["be", 0.3718, 0.0816, 0.382, 0.0915], ["necessary,", 0.386, 0.0836, 0.4326, 0.0942], ["if", 0.4367, 0.0816, 0.4428,